{"id":"NCT02131753","title":"Therapy Optimisation for the Treatment of Hairy Cell Leukemia","official":"Therapy Optimisation for the Treatment of Hairy Cell Leukemia","summary":"The trial will test the effectiveness and toxicity of subcutaneous treatment with one cycle of cladribine in patients with hairy cell leukemia requiring treatment.\n\nThey have to be untreated so far or may be pretreated with alpha-interferon.","conditions":["Hairy Cell Leukemia"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Cladribine s.c. injection, HCL treatment"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Patients with histologically verified hairy cell leukemia\n* Presence of hairy cells in the bone marrow and peripheral blood detected by positive TRAP staining and / or co expression if cell surface antigens cluster of differentiation (CD) 19/CD25 or CD19/CD103 (b-ly7)\n* No previous cytostatic treatment (splenectomy or interferon treatment are allowed)\n* Need for treatment\n* Age at least 18 years old\n* General state of health according to WHO 0-2\n* Current histology, not older than 6 months\n* Written consent by patient\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Patients not fulfilling inclusion criteria above\n* Hairy cell leukemia variants (HCL-V): presence of lymphoid cells in bone marrow and / or peripheral blood, which have an intermediate morphology between hairy cells and prolymphocytes (negative TRAP staining and co- expression of CD19/CD103 without CD25\n* Pretreatment with purine analogues or other chemotherapeutics\n* Concomitant corticosteroid therapy\n* Severe dysfunction of the heart (NYHA III or IV), the lung (WHO-Grade III or IV), the liver, except due to lymphoma (bilirubin \\> 2 mg/dl, alkaline phosphatase, glutamate-oxalacetate transaminase and glutamate-pyruvate transaminase \\> 2 x upper limit of normal), the kidneys (creatinin \\> 2 mg/dl or creatinine clearance \\< 50 ml/min), central nervous system diseases including psychoses.\n* Proven HIV infection\n* Active Hepatitis\n* Other florid infections\n* Anamnesis / diagnosis of other malignant disease (other than non-melanoma associated skin tumours or stage 0 in situ carcinoma of the cervix)\n* Pregnant or lactating women","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"90 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":210,"start":"2004-05","pcd":"2025-12","upd":"2024-08-22","sponsor":"University of Giessen","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Mathias J Rummel, Prof PhD · +4964198542 ext. 650 · mathias.rummel@innere.med.uni-giessen.de","Juergen Barth · +4964198542 ext. 603 · juergen.barth@innere.med.uni-giessen.de"],"sites":[{"f":"Community based hemato-oncology medical office","city":"Ansbach","pr":"","zip":"91522","s":"R","lat":49.3048,"lon":10.5931,"c":"Sebastian Müller, PhD"},{"f":"Community based hemato-oncology medical office","city":"Aschaffenburg","pr":"","zip":"63739","s":"R","lat":49.977,"lon":9.1521,"c":"Manfred Welslau, PhD"},{"f":"Rhön-Saale-Klinik gGmbH","city":"Bad Neustadt an der Saale","pr":"","zip":"97616","s":"R","lat":50.3217,"lon":10.2067,"c":"Klaus Wutke, PhD"},{"f":"Community based hemato-oncology medical office","city":"Berlin","pr":"","zip":"10407","s":"R","lat":52.5244,"lon":13.4105,"c":"Herbert Lebahn, PhD"},{"f":"Charité - Universitätsmedizin Berlin","city":"Berlin","pr":"","zip":"12203","s":"R","lat":52.5244,"lon":13.4105,"c":"Eckhard Thiel, Prof PhD"},{"f":"Community based hemato-oncology medical office","city":"Bremen","pr":"","zip":"28209","s":"R","lat":53.0758,"lon":8.8072,"c":"Karl Wietholt, PhD"},{"f":"Community based hemato-oncology medical office","city":"Celle","pr":"","zip":"29221","s":"R","lat":52.6226,"lon":10.0805,"c":"Felix Marquard, PhD"},{"f":"Community based hemato-oncology medical office","city":"Cottbus","pr":"","zip":"03046","s":"R","lat":51.7577,"lon":14.3289,"c":"Ulrich von Grünhagen, PhD"},{"f":"Community based hemato-oncology medical office","city":"Darmstadt","pr":"","zip":"64295","s":"R","lat":49.8717,"lon":8.6